messages:
tess: Noticed parity bug between node and python SDKs around error shapes. Node emits plain Error with message 'server error' and status 502, python emits typed ServerError with code 'ingress.backend_failure' and retry_hint 'transient'. Confusing for sample apps.

omar: ouch. which quickstart are you using? the js one from docs-site?

tess: yes, master quickstart at docs/quickstart/js. Repro: run the websocket stream example and kill the runtime upstream mid-request. Node side just throws GenericError and our sample app shows a 'Retrying...' toast forever.

ravi: We intentionally added typed errors to python earlier. Node implementation didn't get the new cross-language error-spec. That explains mismatch.

elaine: For onboarding we need the same small contract: error object must include `status`, `request_id`, optional `code`, and stable `retry_hint` values. Sample apps should rely on `retry_hint` rather than trying to parse freeform messages.

tess: proposing change: Node SDK to adopt Error subclassing (AuthError, ClientError, ServerError) and attach these fields: `{status: number, request_id: string, code?: string, retry_hint: 'none'|'refresh_token'|'rate_limit'|'transient'}`. Also add `error.isRetryable()` method.

omar: +1. Also for streams: if an error occurs mid-stream SDK should emit an `error` event with the typed error and a terminal `close` event. No auto-resume for 4xx or errors with retry_hint='none' or 'refresh_token' (unless app calls refresh).

ravi: small nuance: some infra layers rewrite 401->502. SDKs should prefer `code` when present, then status, then message regex. Runtime team: can we standardize a short set of codes for common things: `auth.invalid_token`, `quota.exceeded`, `ingress.backend_failure`?

elaine: PM note: we need to update quickstart examples to handle these explicitly. Show a snippet for Node streaming error handling.

`tess` pasted snippet:

```js
try {
  const stream = client.streamGenerate(prompt);
  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    render(chunk);
  }
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'auth.invalid_token' || err instanceof AuthError) {
    await auth.refresh();
    // optionally retry once
  } else if (err.retry_hint === 'rate_limit') {
    showUpgradeBanner();
  } else if (err.retry_hint === 'transient') {
    // backoff and retry logic
  } else {
    captureException(err);
    throw err;
  }
}
```

elaine: Nice. Action items: (1) eng-runtime to produce code+retry_hint+request_id in structured error JSON (issue runtime#489), (2) node-sdk to add typed error classes + isRetryable util (PR node-sdk#198), (3) docs to update quickstart with the snippet and mention stream terminal semantics.

ravi: I'll open a small cross-language spec PR that enumerates codes and retry_hint values. We should include tests to assert mapping for proxy-rewritten responses.

omar: created issues/PRs: runtime#489, node-sdk#198 (draft). sdk-bot: linked runtime#489 and node-sdk#198.

tess: I'll patch the docs sample app to show explicit handling and add integration test to CI that simulates upstream kill.

elaine: putting this on the onboarding tracker and marking P1 for quickstart docs. PM follow-up after spec PR merges.

ravi: one more ask: please ensure error objects are JSON-serializable and safe to send to browser console (no circulars). Some of our current Error subclasses lose `stack` when serialized.

omar: good catch. We'll attach `toJSON()` that includes message, code, status, request_id, retry_hint.

sdk-bot: New issue created: runtime#489 by ravi. New PR opened: node-sdk#198 by omar (draft).
